le to watch it uncensored.","But the plan's future is uncertain. CNN reported on October 10 that Army and Pentagon officials were caught off guard by the announcement, and Vice President JD Vance publicly cast doubt on it, saying he did not know whether the livestream would actually happen."],"breaking":false,"category":"US","editorPick":false,"headline":"Pentagon Says Fort Hood Shooter's Firing-Squad Execution Will Be Livestreamed — but Doubts Emerge","id":"art-0034-fort-hood-firing-squad-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a judge's gavel and the scales of justice with a December calendar page, abstract and non-violent","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-firing-squad-execution-20261011.webp"},"pinUrl":"","pinned":false,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"pentagon-livestream-firing-squad-execution-fort-hood-2026","socialHeadline":"Pentagon plans to livestream Fort Hood shooter's firing-squad execution — Vance casts doubt","sources":[{"name":"CNN — 'Hegseth vows to make first firing squad execution in decades public' (2026-10-08)","role":"primary","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/08/politics/pete-hegseth-vows-to-make-first-firing-squad-execution-in-decades-public"},{"name":"AP/NPR — 'Pentagon says the firing squad execution of Fort Hood shooter will be livestreamed' (2026-10-09)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.wextradio.org/npr-news/2026-10-09/pentagon-says-the-firing-squad-execution-of-fort-hood-shooter-will-be-livestreamed"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["Fort Hood","Nidal Hasan","Pentagon","Death Penalty","Pete Hegseth"],"verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:00Z","chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"eventConfirmed":true,"imageChecked":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"notes":"Verified via CNN and AP/NPR page reads: Pentagon (Oct 8/9) said Dec 3, 2026 firing-squad execution of Nidal Hasan (convicted 2013, 13 murders + 32 attempted murders, 2009 Fort Hood attack) will be livestreamed; Hegseth to podcaster Jack Posobiec aboard USS Abraham Lincoln (Oct 7): 'people are able to watch it'; Acting Army Secretary Adam Telle set Dec 3, 1pm local; Trump approved; first US military execution in 60+ years, first by firing squad since WWII; survivor Alonzo Lunsford supports. IMPORTANT CAVEAT included in article: CNN Oct 10 — Army/Pentagon caught off guard, VP Vance cast doubt on whether it will happen.","primarySourceFound":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","supersededChecked":true}},{"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","body":["Eliud Kipchoge ended a three-year wait for a marathon victory in emphatic fashion on Sunday, winning the Melbourne Marathon in a course-record 2:09:10.","The 41-year-old Kenyan broke away from the field inside the final 10 kilometres and crossed the line two seconds inside the previous race record of 2:09:12, set by Timothy Ronoh in 2022. It was Kipchoge's 17th career marathon victory — and his first since Berlin in September 2023.","The race, which began at 6:15 a.m. local time, finished with a half-lap inside the Melbourne Cricket Ground, where Kipchoge soaked in the applause of the home crowd.","Australia's Thomas Do Canto finished second in 2:10:35, with compatriot Reece Edwards third in 2:14:33. New Zealand's Camille French won the women's race in 2:28:25. For Kipchoge, the two-time Olympic champion widely regarded as the greatest marathoner in history, the win marks a striking late-career resurgence at 41."],"breaking":false,"category":"Sports","editorPick":false,"headline":"Eliud Kipchoge, 41, Ends Three-Year Drought With Melbourne Marathon Win in Course Record","id":"art-0035-kipchoge-melbourne-2026","image":{"alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a marathon runner silhouette with a stopwatch showing 2:09:10 and a finish-line ribbon","caption":"Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration","src":"/images/media-generation-nv-kipchoge-melbourne-20261011.webp"},"pinUrl":"","pinned":false,"publishedAt":"2026-10-11T13:45:00Z","slug":"eliud-kipchoge-wins-melbourne-marathon-course-record-2026","socialHeadline":"Kipchoge wins Melbourne Marathon in course-record 2:09:10 — first win since 2023","sources":[{"name":"Reuters — 'Kipchoge wins first marathon in three years in Melbourne' (2026-10-11)","role":"primary","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/kipchoge-wins-first-marathon-three-years-melbourne-2026-10-11/"},{"name":"Associated Press — Melbourne Marathon 2026 results (2026-10-11)","role":"corroboration","url":"https://www.europesays.com/australia/117924/"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["Eliud Kipchoge","Marathon","Melbourne","Athletics","Kenya"],"verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:00Z","chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"eventConfirmed":true,"imageChecked":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"notes":"Verified via Reuters and AP page reads: Melbourne Marathon, Sunday Oct 11, 2026; Eliud Kipchoge (Kenya, 41) won in 2:09:10, new course record (old 2:09:12, Timothy Ronoh, 2022); 17th marathon win; first since Berlin Sep 2023; 2nd Thomas Do Canto (AUS) 2:10:35; 3rd Reece Edwards (AUS) 2:14:33; women's winner Camille French (NZL) 2:28:25; finished with half-lap inside the MCG.","primarySourceFound":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","supersededChecked":true}},{"id":"art-0036-commanders-giants-ot-tie-2026","slug":"giants-commanders-27-27-overtime-tie-daniels","headline":"Commanders Botch Final Play as Clock Runs Out, Settling for 27-27 Tie With Giants","socialHeadline":"Jayden Daniels was sacked with 8 seconds left in OT and no timeouts — a 42-yard field goal never got snapped, and the Giants escaped Landover with a 27-27 tie","summary":"The Washington Commanders reached the Giants' 24-yard line in overtime and were seconds from a winning field goal — but Jayden Daniels was brought down with no timeouts left, the clock expired, and the Week 5 game ended in a 27-27 tie at Northwest Stadium. Daniels took responsibility after the game.","body":["The Washington Commanders had the win in their hands. Driving into New York Giants territory in overtime on Sunday, October 11, they stood 24 yards from the end zone, 8 seconds on the clock, and a 42-yard field goal well within Drew Stevens' range. What followed was one of the most bewildering clock-management failures of the NFL season.","Quarterback Jayden Daniels, on second-and-8 from the Giants' 24, dropped back, scrambled, and was tackled for no gain as the seconds bled away. With no timeouts remaining, the Commanders could not stop the clock or spike the ball. The officials ruled the overtime period over before Washington could run another play — and the Week 5 contest at Northwest Stadium in Landover, Maryland, finished as a 27-27 tie.","\"We have to stop the clock,\" Daniels said afterward. \"We have to know the situation. It starts with everyone, top down. Ultimately, it's on me.\" Head coach Dan Quinn refused to put the sequence on his quarterback, saying the call and the clock management were his responsibility. Quinn said the tie \"feels like a loss.\"","The ending overshadowed a dramatic game. Daniels, returning from a dislocated left elbow suffered in a Week 2 loss to Dallas, completed 17 of 25 passes for 199 yards and rushed for 103 yards and two touchdowns. Washington led 27-13 with just over seven minutes left in regulation before the Giants, behind Jameis Winston, rallied to force overtime.","The tie moved Washington to 1-3-1 on the season, ahead of a Week 6 Monday night visit to the San Francisco 49ers. The Giants stood at 3-1-1. For a league in which ties remain one of the rarest results, this one will be remembered for what happened in the final eight seconds of overtime."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","Washington Commanders","New York Giants","Jayden Daniels","Overtime"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-commanders-ot-tie-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a tied 27-27 overtime scoreboard with a game clock at 0:00 over a stylized football field","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of a tied 27-27 overtime scoreboard with a game clock at 0:00 over a stylized football field. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"ESPN — 'Commanders' Daniels takes blame for botched final play in OT' (Jordan Raanan, 2026-10-11)","url":"https://10bmnews.com/commanders-daniels-takes-blame-for-botched-final-play-in-ot/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Associated Press — 'Daniels, Commanders settle for tie with Giants after botching final play of OT' (via TSN, 2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.tsn.ca/nfl/article/daniels-commanders-settle-for-tie-with-giants-after-botching-final-play-of-ot/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via ESPN (Raanan) and AP page reads: Giants-Commanders 27-27 OT tie, Oct 11 2026, Northwest Stadium Landover (Week 5); Daniels tackled for no gain with 8 seconds left in OT, no timeouts, clock expired before a would-be 42-yard Drew Stevens FG; Daniels: 'Ultimately, it's on me'; Quinn took play-calling blame, tie 'feels like a loss'; Daniels returned from dislocated left elbow (Week 2), 17/25, 199 yds, 103 rushing yds, 2 TDs; records: WAS 1-3-1, NYG 3-1-1. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0037-greenlaw-ejection-49ers-seahawks-2026","slug":"greenlaw-ejected-head-butt-seahawks-32-29","headline":"Dre Greenlaw Ejected for Head-Butting Helmetless Ernest Jones IV as 49ers Edge Seahawks 32-29","socialHeadline":"The 49ers linebacker was disqualified in the second quarter after a late hit on Sam Darnold and a head-butt on a helmetless Ernest Jones IV — but San Francisco stayed unbeaten with a 32-29 win in Seattle","summary":"San Francisco stayed undefeated with a 32-29 win over Seattle on Sunday, but lost linebacker Dre Greenlaw to a second-quarter ejection after a late hit on Sam Darnold was followed by a head-butt on helmetless Seahawks linebacker Ernest Jones IV. Seattle committed four turnovers.","body":["The San Francisco 49ers survived their own linebacker's temper on Sunday, beating the Seattle Seahawks 32-29 at Lumen Field to remain undefeated — despite losing Dre Greenlaw to an ejection midway through the second quarter.","The sequence began with a late hit by Greenlaw on Seahawks quarterback Sam Darnold near the sideline, which drew an unnecessary-roughness flag. As pushing and shoving broke out on the Seattle sideline, Greenlaw — still wearing his helmet — head-butted Seahawks linebacker Ernest Jones IV, who was not wearing his. Officials disqualified Greenlaw from the game, ending his afternoon.","The ejection could easily have tilted the NFC West showdown toward Seattle. Instead, San Francisco's defense forced four turnovers. A fumble at the goal line recovered in the end zone by rookie defensive tackle Gracen Halton just before halftime gave the 49ers a 21-13 lead they would not surrender.","Seattle fought back: Jaxon Smith-Njigba's 16-yard touchdown put the Seahawks ahead 23-21 in the third quarter, and Jason Myers' kicking kept it close late. But the 49ers' takeaways proved decisive in the 32-29 final.","Greenlaw's ejection adds to a heated chapter of the 49ers-Seahawks rivalry. No suspension had been announced as of publication, and this story makes no claim about further league discipline."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","San Francisco 49ers","Seattle Seahawks","Dre Greenlaw","Ejection"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-greenlaw-ejection-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of two stylized football helmets colliding, a referee penalty flag and a red ejection whistle motif","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of two stylized football helmets colliding, a referee penalty flag and a red ejection whistle motif. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — '49ers capitalize on four turnovers to down Seahawks, remain undefeated' (2026-10-12)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/nfl/49ers-capitalize-four-turnovers-down-seahawks-remain-undefeated--flm-2026-10-12/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Sporting News — 'Why Dre Greenlaw was ejected from Seahawks-49ers' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.sportingnews.com/us/nfl/news/dre-greenlaw-ejected-seahawks-49ers-confrontation-ernest-jones/ddd16b3af9c431af7e947309","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via Reuters game report and Sporting News page reads: 49ers beat Seahawks 32-29 in Seattle, Oct 11 2026 (Week 5); Greenlaw ejected in 2nd quarter after late hit on Darnold near sideline, then head-butted helmetless LB Ernest Jones IV; Seattle committed 4 turnovers; 49ers remain undefeated; Halton goal-line fumble recovery TD before halftime. Suspension speculation unconfirmed — story makes no suspension claim. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0038-packers-bears-burden-quit-2026","slug":"packers-beat-bears-31-7-burden-quit","headline":"Packers Maul Bears 31-7, Then Fire Back at Luther Burden III: 'He Quit'","socialHeadline":"Green Bay backed up its pregame talk with a 31-7 rout at Lambeau, then answered Bears receiver Luther Burden III's 'make them quit' vow — as Chicago played without injured Caleb Williams","summary":"The Green Bay Packers thrashed the Chicago Bears 31-7 at Lambeau Field on Sunday, then delivered the verbal knockout. Linebacker Zaire Franklin fired back at Bears receiver Luther Burden III, who had promised before the game to 'beat them real bad and make them quit' — 'He quit today,' Franklin said. Chicago played without injured quarterback Caleb Williams.","body":["The talking started before kickoff. Chicago Bears receiver Luther Burden III vowed his team would \"beat them real bad and make them quit\" when the Bears visited Lambeau Field on Sunday. The Green Bay Packers heard it — and made the trash talk their motivation in a 31-7 Week 5 rout on October 11, 2026.","After the game, Packers linebacker Zaire Franklin delivered the rebuttal. \"He quit today,\" Franklin said of Burden, turning the receiver's own vow back on him after Green Bay dominated in all phases.","The Bears were also shorthanded where it mattered most. With starting quarterback Caleb Williams injured, Chicago turned to backup Tyson Bagent, and the offense never found its rhythm against a Packers defense that fed off the home crowd.","The 31-7 final was a statement in the NFC North's oldest rivalry — and a reminder that pregame guarantees only count if you back them up. Burden and the Bears learned that lesson the hard way at Lambeau."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","Green Bay Packers","Chicago Bears","Luther Burden","Rivalry"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-packers-bears-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a 31-7 final score with Week 5 tag, green-gold and navy-orange bars and a stylized football","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of a 31-7 final score with Week 5 tag, green-gold and navy-orange bars and a stylized football. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"ESPN — 'Packers maul Bears, fire back at Burden quit talk' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.espn.ph/nfl/story/_/id/50162146/packers-maul-bears-fire-back-burden-quit-talk","role":"primary"},{"name":"NBC Sports — 'Packers LB Zaire Franklin: Luther Burden said he'd make us quit, but he quit Sunday' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/packers-lb-zaire-franklin-luther-burden-said-hed-make-us-quit-but-he-quit-sunday","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via ESPN and NBC Sports page reads: Packers beat Bears 31-7 at Lambeau, Week 5, Oct 11 2026; LB Zaire Franklin's 'He quit today' response to WR Luther Burden III's pregame 'beat them real bad and make them quit' vow; Bears started Tyson Bagent for injured Caleb Williams. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0039-big-ten-oregon-ucla-spot-2026","slug":"big-ten-admits-error-oregon-ucla-2-point-conversion","headline":"Big Ten Admits Officials Spotted Ball Wrong on Oregon's Do-or-Die 2-Point Try in 17-15 Loss to UCLA","socialHeadline":"The conference said the ball should have been spotted at the half-yard line — not the 1.5-yard line — for Oregon's tying attempt with 2:16 left. The Ducks were stuffed, and UCLA held on to win at Autzen.","summary":"The Big Ten admitted on Sunday that officials incorrectly spotted the ball on Oregon's tying 2-point conversion attempt with 2:16 left in a 17-15 loss to UCLA at Autzen Stadium. The ball was placed at the 1.5-yard line instead of the half-yard line after a UCLA facemask penalty — and the Ducks were stopped short.","body":["One yard. That was the difference the Big Ten admitted to on Sunday, October 11, a day after the Oregon Ducks fell 17-15 to the UCLA Bruins at Autzen Stadium.","With 2:16 left in the fourth quarter, Oregon quarterback Brock Thomas ran up the middle on a first 2-point try and was stopped — but UCLA linebacker Sammy Omosigho grabbed his facemask, drawing a personal foul. The penalty should have moved the ball half the distance to the goal from the end of the run: the half-yard line. Instead, officials spotted it from the original line of scrimmage, placing it at the 1.5-yard line.","In a statement released through ESPN's Pete Thamel, the conference confirmed the error. The ball should have been spotted, in the conference's words, half the distance to the goal from the end of the run of the first attempt — not from where the play started.","Given the second chance from the 1.5-yard line, Oregon handed to running back Jordon Davison, who was stuffed by defensive tackle Tyson Ford short of the goal line. The Ducks' last-gasp lateral play on the final snap ended with a fumble recovered by UCLA's Dante Lovett.","The Bruins improved to 5-0 and climbed to No. 12 in the Associated Press rankings, while Oregon fell to 3-2 — its second loss of the season. Whether the misplaced spot changed the outcome will be debated all week; the admission itself, rare for the conference, is already fueling the argument."],"category":"Sports","tags":["College Football","Oregon Ducks","UCLA Bruins","Big Ten","Officiating"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-big-ten-spot-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a football under a magnifying glass at the half-yard line with 2:16 remaining on a 2-point conversion","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of a football under a magnifying glass at the half-yard line with 2:16 remaining on a 2-point conversion. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Sports Illustrated — 'Big Ten Admits Officiating Mistake in Crucial Play of Oregon's Loss to UCLA Bruins' (2026-10-11, quoting full Big Ten statement via ESPN's Pete Thamel)","url":"https://www.si.com/college/oregon/football/big-ten-admits-officiating-mistake-crucial-play-oregon-ducks-loss-ucla-bruins","role":"primary"},{"name":"USA Today — 'Big Ten releases statement on critical officiating mistake in Oregon-UCLA' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://duckswire.usatoday.com/story/sports/college/ducks/football/2026/10/11/oregon-football-big-ten-makes-statement-officiating-mistake-ucla/92209464007/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via SI (quoting full Big Ten statement) and USA Today page reads: UCLA beat Oregon 17-15 at Autzen, Oct 10 2026; Big Ten admitted Oct 11 that officials spotted ball at 1.5-yard line instead of half-yard line for Oregon's 2nd 2-point attempt with 2:16 left, after UCLA facemask on Brock Thomas (Omosigho) on first attempt; Jordon Davison stuffed by Tyson Ford on retry; UCLA first win at Autzen since 2004, 5-0 / AP No. 12; Oregon 3-2, second loss. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0040-mendoza-nfl-debut-raiders-2026","slug":"fernando-mendoza-nfl-debut-raiders-patriots","headline":"No. 1 Pick Fernando Mendoza Makes NFL Debut in Raiders' 45-17 Loss to Patriots","socialHeadline":"The 2026 top draft pick entered late at Gillette Stadium, going 6-of-8 for 48 yards in mop-up duty. Coach Klint Kubiak: 'He did a good job.'","summary":"The 2026 No. 1 overall pick is officially an NFL quarterback. Fernando Mendoza made his regular-season debut for the Las Vegas Raiders on Sunday, entering late in a 45-17 loss to the New England Patriots at Gillette Stadium. The rookie completed 6 of 8 passes for 48 yards, and coach Klint Kubiak praised his first outing.","body":["It came in garbage time, but it was history. With about six minutes left on Sunday and the Las Vegas Raiders trailing the New England Patriots 45-17 at Gillette Stadium, the 2026 No. 1 overall pick jogged onto the field for his first NFL regular-season action.","Fernando Mendoza, the Raiders' franchise hope from the 2026 draft, operated the offense calmly in his brief stint, completing 6 of 8 passes for 48 yards against a Patriots defense protecting a 28-point lead.","Head coach Klint Kubiak liked what he saw. \"He did a good job,\" Kubiak said of the rookie's first taste of NFL speed.","The result itself was never in doubt — the Patriots controlled the Week 5 game throughout on October 11. But for Raiders fans, the scoreline was secondary. The debut of the No. 1 pick, however brief, was the moment that mattered, and Mendoza now has his first NFL snaps in the books."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","Las Vegas Raiders","New England Patriots","Fernando Mendoza","NFL Draft"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-mendoza-debut-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of a stylized quarterback silhouette with No. 1 pick and NFL debut motifs","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of a stylized quarterback silhouette with No. 1 pick and NFL debut motifs. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"ESPN — 'Raiders QB Fernando Mendoza makes NFL regular-season debut in late loss to Patriots' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.espn.ph/nfl/story/_/id/50161581/raiders-qb-fernando-mendoza-makes-nfl-regular-season-debut-late-loss-patriots","role":"primary"},{"name":"USA Today — 'Fernando Mendoza Raiders NFL debut' (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nfl/patriots/2026/10/11/fernando-mendoza-raiders-nfl-debut/92207222007/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via ESPN and USA Today page reads: 2026 No. 1 overall pick Fernando Mendoza debuted for Raiders late in 45-17 loss to Patriots at Gillette Stadium, Week 5, Oct 11 2026; entered with ~6:00 left down 28; 6-of-8, 48 yards; coach Klint Kubiak: 'He did a good job.' No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0041-asia-markets-earnings-oil-2026","slug":"asia-shares-cautious-earnings-season-oil-slips","headline":"Asian Shares Open Cautiously as Earnings Season Looms and Oil Slips","socialHeadline":"Investors stayed on the sidelines Monday ahead of the US earnings season, with South Korea down 1.1% and crude sliding on confusion over an unconfirmed Trump energy-ceasefire claim and Gulf strikes","summary":"Asian shares started Monday cautiously as investors braced for the US earnings season, which kicks off with the big banks on Tuesday. South Korea fell 1.1%, while oil slid — Brent down 1.1% to $103.50 and US crude 1.2% lower at $90.73 — amid confusion over an unconfirmed Trump energy-ceasefire announcement and strikes in the Gulf.","body":["Asian markets opened the week on a cautious note on Monday, October 12, with investors holding back ahead of the US third-quarter earnings season. America's biggest banks report on Tuesday, setting the tone for a reporting season Wall Street will read closely for signs of how the economy is weathering the autumn.","South Korea was among the region's weakest performers, dropping 1.1% as the defensive mood spread across the region's trading floors.","Energy markets added to the uncertainty. Brent crude slipped 1.1% to $103.50 a barrel and US crude fell 1.2% to $90.73, as traders weighed confusion over an unconfirmed energy-ceasefire announcement by US President Donald Trump against reports of continued strikes in the Gulf.","With earnings, energy headlines, and geopolitics all pulling in different directions, Monday's session set up a week where Asian markets will take their cues from Wall Street's results as much as from their own fundamentals."],"category":"Business","tags":["Markets","Asia","Stocks","Oil","Earnings"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-asia-markets-20261011.webp","alt":"Flat editorial illustration of candlestick stock charts, an Asia map outline and an oil barrel with a downward arrow","caption":"Illustration: Flat editorial illustration of candlestick stock charts, an Asia map outline and an oil barrel with a downward arrow. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Reuters — 'Global markets: Shares cautious in Asia as earnings loom, oil slips' (2026-10-12)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/china/global-markets-wrapup-1-2026-10-12/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Devdiscourse — 'Global Markets: Shares cautious in Asia as earnings loom, oil slips' (2026-10-12)","url":"https://www.devdiscourse.com/article/international/3990565-global-markets-shares-cautious-in-asia-as-earnings-loom-oil-slips","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Verified via Reuters wire and Devdiscourse page reads: Asian shares cautious Monday Oct 12 ahead of US earnings season (banks Tuesday); South Korea -1.1%; Brent -1.1% to $103.50, US crude -1.2% to $90.73, on confusion over Trump's unconfirmed energy-ceasefire claim and Gulf strikes. Ephemeral daily wire. No newer development.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T01:18:17Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0042-brewers-dodgers-nlcs-game1-2026","slug":"brewers-edge-dodgers-2-1-nlcs-game-1-turang-homer","headline":"Brewers Edge Dodgers 2-1 in NLCS Game 1 Behind Turang Homer and Shutdown Bullpen","socialHeadline":"Turang's 4th-inning homer and 4 2/3 scoreless bullpen innings gave Milwaukee a 2-1 NLCS Game 1 win over the Dodgers","summary":"The Milwaukee Brewers took Game 1 of the National League Championship Series 2-1 over the Los Angeles Dodgers on October 11, riding Brice Turang's tying home run, rookie Luis Lara's go-ahead single and 4 2/3 scoreless innings from their bullpen at American Family Field.","body":["The Milwaukee Brewers drew first blood in the National League Championship Series on Saturday, October 11, 2026, defeating the Los Angeles Dodgers 2-1 in Game 1 at American Family Field. It was the first NLCS meeting of two 100-win teams since the 1976 Reds and Phillies, and it lived up to the billing as a pitchers' duel.","Brice Turang provided the first breakthrough, launching a 384-foot home run to left-center off Tarik Skubal in the fourth inning to erase a 1-0 deficit. An inning later, rookie Luis Lara delivered the decisive blow: with Garrett Mitchell aboard after a walk and moved up on Cooper Pratt's sacrifice bunt, Lara lined a tiebreaking RBI single off Skubal to put Milwaukee ahead 2-1.","The Brewers' bullpen made the slim lead stand up. D.L. Hall, Abner Uribe, Aaron Ashby and Trevor Megill combined for 4 2/3 scoreless innings, with Megill surviving two ninth-inning walks to earn the save when Mookie Betts flied out to end it. The victory snapped Milwaukee's seven-game postseason losing streak against the Dodgers, who swept them in last year's NLCS.","Skubal, the two-time AL Cy Young winner acquired from Detroit at the trade deadline, took the loss despite striking out seven over five innings, allowing two runs on five hits with two walks. It was only his second defeat in eight career postseason starts. The Dodgers' lone run came on Andy Pages' second-inning RBI single that scored Shohei Ohtani; Los Angeles went 1-for-6 with runners in scoring position, grounded into three double plays and stranded nine runners.","A crowd of 42,617 watched the opener. Game 2 is set for Monday, October 12, in Milwaukee, with Yoshinobu Yamamoto scheduled for the Dodgers against Logan Henderson for the Brewers."],"category":"Sports","tags":["MLB","NLCS","Milwaukee Brewers","Los Angeles Dodgers","Brice Turang"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-brewers-dodgers-nlcs-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated scoreboard showing Brewers 2, Dodgers 1 in NLCS Game 1","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated scoreboard showing Brewers 2, Dodgers 1 in NLCS Game 1. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Associated Press — Brewers 2, Dodgers 1, NLCS Game 1 (2026-10-11)","url":"https://apnews.com/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — NLCS Game 1 report (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"AP game story as primary; Reuters and Sportradar box-score data corroborate score, scorers, pitching lines and Game 2 matchup. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0043-ravens-falcons-ot-2026","slug":"ravens-beat-falcons-30-23-ot-huntley-penix-injured","headline":"Huntley Stars as Ravens Stun Falcons 30-23 in Overtime; Penix Exits With Rib Injury","socialHeadline":"Backup QB Tyler Huntley threw for 201 yards and 2 TDs and ran in the OT winner as Baltimore beat Atlanta 30-23; Michael Penix Jr. left late with a rib injury","summary":"The Baltimore Ravens beat the Atlanta Falcons 30-23 in overtime on Sunday night, October 11, as backup quarterback Tyler Huntley threw for 201 yards and two touchdowns and scored the winning touchdown on a 1-yard run. Falcons starter Michael Penix Jr. left the game late in regulation with a rib injury.","body":["The Baltimore Ravens needed overtime and their backup quarterback to escape Atlanta with a 30-23 victory over the Falcons on Sunday night, October 11, 2026, at Mercedes-Benz Stadium. Tyler Huntley, starting in place of the injured Lamar Jackson (ankle), completed 24 of 32 passes for 201 yards and two touchdowns, then capped the opening drive of overtime with a 1-yard touchdown run with 2:57 remaining.","The comeback began with Baltimore trailing 23-15 and only 2:25 left in regulation. Huntley engineered a six-play, 71-yard drive, finding Devontez Walker for a 7-yard touchdown with 40 seconds left before Derrick Henry took a direct snap for the tying two-point conversion. In overtime, safety Kyle Hamilton intercepted Falcons backup Tua Tagovailoa to seal the win.","The Falcons lost more than the game. Starting quarterback Michael Penix Jr. was sacked by Tavius Robinson with 27 seconds left in a tie game and suffered a rib injury. Penix walked off under his own power and was listed as questionable; he briefly re-entered for one play, which fell incomplete, then watched overtime from the sideline with a towel over his head as Tagovailoa finished the game in his Falcons debut. Penix finished 19 of 32 for 240 yards and a touchdown and said afterward he does not expect the injury to be a long-term issue and hopes to play next week.","Derrick Henry powered the Ravens with 102 rushing yards plus an 18-yard touchdown reception, while Drake London caught seven passes for 118 yards for Atlanta. Jessie Bates III returned a fumble 36 yards for a Falcons touchdown in the first quarter. Ravens coach Jesse Minter publicly praised Huntley's performance after the game.","The win moved Baltimore to 4-1 and into sole possession of first place in the AFC North. Atlanta fell to 2-3."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NFL","Baltimore Ravens","Atlanta Falcons","Tyler Huntley","Michael Penix Jr."],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-ravens-falcons-ot-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated scoreboard showing Ravens 30, Falcons 23 in overtime","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated scoreboard showing Ravens 30, Falcons 23 in overtime. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Associated Press — Ravens 30, Falcons 23 OT game story (2026-10-11)","url":"https://apnews.com/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — Ravens-Falcons Week 5 report (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/","role":"corroboration"},{"name":"NBC Sports — Ravens-Falcons coverage (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"AP game story as primary; Reuters and NBC Sports corroborate score, stats, injury sequence and standings. Penix long-term outlook is his own attributed statement, not a medical fact. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0044-trump-energy-ceasefire-2026","slug":"trump-claims-energy-ceasefire-ukraine-russia-oil-falls","headline":"Trump Claims Ukraine-Russia 'Energy Ceasefire' Agreed; Oil Prices Fall as Neither Side Confirms","socialHeadline":"Trump announced an 'energy ceasefire' on Truth Social; oil fell Monday, but Ukraine said it was awaiting details and Russia has not commented","summary":"US President Donald Trump announced on Sunday, October 11, that Ukraine and Russia had agreed to an immediate \"energy ceasefire.\" Oil prices fell on Monday, but neither Kyiv nor Moscow confirmed any agreement, with Ukraine's president saying the announcement was news to him.","body":["US President Donald Trump declared on his Truth Social platform on Sunday, October 11, 2026, that Ukraine and Russia had agreed to an immediate halt to strikes on energy infrastructure. \"Effective immediately, there is an ENERGY CEASEFIRE in the War between Russia and Ukraine. Both parties have agreed. Do not break it!\" he wrote, according to reporting by CNN.","Oil markets reacted on Monday: Brent crude fell $1.54, or 1.47%, to $103.18 a barrel, while US West Texas Intermediate dropped 1.68% to $90.31 and ICE gasoil slipped 3% to $1,436, Reuters reported. But the supposed agreement itself remained unverified. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy told Axios the announcement was \"news for me,\" and later posted that Ukraine supports a ceasefire but is \"awaiting details from the American side.\" Russia has not commented at all.","The announcement came days after a controversial diesel arrangement under which Russia is to immediately supply more than 300,000 metric tons (2.25 million barrels) of diesel, followed by 500,000 tons in November and one million tons afterward, with temporary US sanctions relief, according to Fox News and CNN reporting. IEA chief Fatih Birol on Sunday urged member countries to assess possible diesel releases.","Analysts urged caution. \"Questions remain over the validity and longevity of any such ceasefire... without clearer evidence that it will actually hold, the extent of the pullback is likely to stay limited,\" analyst Tim Waterer said, as quoted by Reuters. The continuing Middle East conflict is meanwhile keeping Brent above $100 a barrel.","NewsVeria notes: as of publication, the \"energy ceasefire\" exists only as a claim by President Trump. No confirmation has come from Ukraine or Russia, and readers should treat it as unconfirmed until independently verified by the parties involved."],"category":"World","tags":["Donald Trump","Ukraine","Russia","Oil Prices","Energy"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-energy-ceasefire-oil-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated oil barrels with a falling price arrow","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated oil barrels with a falling price arrow. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Donald Trump — Truth Social post (2026-10-11), via CNN","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/11/politics/trump-ukraine-russia-energy-ceasefire","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — oil market report (2026-10-12)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/markets/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Trump's Truth Social post (quoted by CNN) is the primary source for the announcement; Reuters market data corroborates the oil-price move. Framing is mandatory: presented strictly as an unconfirmed claim — neither Ukraine nor Russia has confirmed any agreement. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0045-saudi-travel-warnings-2026","slug":"travel-warnings-saudi-arabia-houthi-airport-attacks","headline":"Seven Countries Issue Travel Warnings for Saudi Arabia After Houthi Airport Attacks","socialHeadline":"The US, UK, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand advised against travel to parts of Saudi Arabia after a wave of attacks on Saudi airports","summary":"Seven countries — the United States, United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand — have issued travel advisories against Saudi Arabia following a series of Houthi attacks on Saudi airports, including strikes that closed major airports and killed more than a dozen people, according to Saudi authorities.","body":["Governments around the world moved on Sunday and Monday to warn their citizens against travel to Saudi Arabia after a wave of attacks on the kingdom's airports claimed by Yemen's Houthi movement. The United States, United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand all issued or updated advisories, Al Jazeera reported.","The advisories vary in scope. Australia's Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade told citizens to avoid Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport and reconsider travel to other Saudi airports. New Zealand advised against all travel to the Riyadh airport and the Najran, Jazan and Asir provinces. The US Embassy in Riyadh on Sunday advised Americans to reconsider travel, citing Iranian and Houthi threats. Canada advised against non-essential travel to any part of Saudi Arabia, South Korea urged citizens to leave unless on essential business, and Britain advised against travel to Jeddah and Dammam and all airports except Medina's except for essential reasons.","The warnings follow five attacks on Saudi airports in under a week. King Khalid and King Fahd international airports were closed. The Houthis claimed the four strikes before Sunday's, which went unclaimed. Saudi Arabia's civil aviation authority said Sunday's attack killed one person and injured 11. For Saturday's attack, Saudi authorities reported 12 dead and more than 300 wounded, according to Reuters; Al Jazeera reported 13 killed, a small discrepancy between outlets. The dead included four Saudis and two Bangladeshis, plus American, Jordanian, Palestinian, Syrian, Sudanese and Egyptian nationals, according to Saudi authorities via Reuters.","Reuters separately reported that Yemen's Houthis renewed their warning over Saudi airports after the deadly Riyadh attack, signalling the threat to aviation remains active."],"category":"World","tags":["Saudi Arabia","Houthis","Travel Advisory","Yemen","Aviation"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-saudi-travel-warning-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated airplane over a desert airport with a warning sign","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated airplane over a desert airport with a warning sign. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Government travel advisories — US State Dept, UK FCDO, Australia DFAT, NZ MFAT, Global Affairs Canada, ROK MFA (2026-10-11/12), via Al Jazeera","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/10/12/countries-warn-against-travel-to-saudi-arabia-following-houthi-attacks","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — Houthis renew warning over Saudi airports (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/yemens-houthis-renew-warning-over-saudi-airports-after-deadly-riyadh-attack-2026-10-11/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Primary: the government advisories themselves (quoted via Al Jazeera's roundup); corroboration: Reuters on the attacks and Houthi warning. Casualty figures attributed to Saudi authorities; small Reuters/Al Jazeera discrepancy on Saturday's toll noted. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0046-china-sanctions-taiwan-2026","slug":"china-sanctions-paraguay-belize-ministers-taiwan-ties","headline":"China Sanctions Paraguay and Belize Ministers Over Taiwan Ties","socialHeadline":"Beijing froze assets and barred entry for Paraguay's communications minister and Belize's foreign minister, citing their countries' diplomatic relations with Taiwan","summary":"China's Foreign Ministry announced on Monday, October 12, 2026, sanctions against Paraguay's communications minister Gustavo Villate and Belize's foreign minister Francis Fonseca over their countries' diplomatic ties with Taiwan, freezing any assets they hold in China and barring them from Hong Kong and Macau.","body":["China announced sanctions on Monday against two Latin American ministers — Paraguay's Communications Minister Gustavo Villate and Belize's Foreign Minister Francis Fonseca — in retaliation for their countries' diplomatic relations with Taiwan, Reuters reported. The measures take effect immediately.","Under the two notices issued by the Foreign Ministry in Beijing, any assets the ministers hold in China will be frozen, they will be denied entry visas to Hong Kong and Macau, and Chinese organisations and individuals will be barred from transactions or cooperation with them. The ministry cited national sovereignty and security and opposition to \"Taiwan separatist activities,\" blaming \"certain anti-China politicians... driven by self-interest\" for pushing nations to maintain ties with Taipei.","Paraguay and Belize are two of only 12 countries worldwide that maintain formal diplomatic relations with Taiwan. The announcement came two days after Taiwan's National Day on October 10: Villate had marked the occasion on social media, while Belize's embassy in Taiwan celebrated the 37th anniversary of bilateral ties. Taiwan's Foreign Minister Lin Chia-lung visited Belize last month, and Villate met Taiwan's deputy foreign minister Chen Ming-chi in June.","Reuters noted the sanctions are largely symbolic, as such ministers rarely travel to China, and that Beijing has previously applied similar measures to Western politicians."],"category":"World","tags":["China","Taiwan","Paraguay","Belize","Sanctions"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-china-sanctions-taiwan-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated diplomatic folders with flag pins and a sanction stamp motif","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated diplomatic folders with flag pins and a sanction stamp motif. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs — sanctions notices (2026-10-12), via Reuters","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/china/china-sanctions-paraguay-belize-ministers-over-taiwan-ties-2026-10-12/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — China sanctions Paraguay, Belize ministers (2026-10-12)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/china/china-sanctions-paraguay-belize-ministers-over-taiwan-ties-2026-10-12/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Primary: Chinese MFA announcements (two notices, Oct 12); corroboration: Reuters Beijing report with names, measures and context. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0047-hurricane-simon-2026","slug":"hurricane-simon-weakens-category-3-mexico-coast","headline":"Hurricane Simon Weakens to Category 3 Off Mexico's Pacific Coast; Flooding Rains Lash Jalisco and Colima","socialHeadline":"Simon dropped from Category 4 to Category 3 on October 11 and is forecast to keep weakening, but Mexico warns of life-threatening flooding and mudslides","summary":"Hurricane Simon weakened from a Category 4 to a Category 3 storm off Mexico's Pacific coast on Sunday, October 11, 2026, and is forecast to continue weakening this week — but Mexican authorities warned of life-threatening flooding, mudslides and storm surge as heavy rains battered coastal states.","body":["Hurricane Simon lost strength on Sunday as it tracked parallel to Mexico's Pacific coastline. The storm packed 145 mph (230 km/h) winds as a Category 4 hurricane around 9 a.m. local time, centered about 105 km west-northwest of Manzanillo, Colima, before weakening to Category 3 with 205 km/h winds by Sunday evening, according to the US National Hurricane Center.","In its latest advisory (Advisory 19, issued around 2:57 a.m. UTC on October 12), the NHC placed Simon about 45 miles south-southwest of Cabo Corrientes with maximum sustained winds of 120 mph and a central pressure of 956 millibars, moving northwest at 5 mph. Forecasters expect continued weakening — to around 100 mph Monday, 90 mph Tuesday, and Category 1 strength near Mazatlan, Sinaloa, by Wednesday before becoming post-tropical Thursday. It remains uncertain whether the storm's center will cross inland or stay offshore.","The greater danger is water, not wind. The NHC forecast an additional 50 to 100 mm of rain for Colima, Jalisco, Nayarit and Sinaloa, with isolated totals up to 200 mm and storm-total accumulations reaching 762 mm in parts of Michoacan, Colima and Jalisco — raising the risk of life-threatening flash flooding, mudslides and storm surge along the coast.","Mexico placed 28 municipalities in Jalisco and Colima under its highest cyclone alert and 93 more on high alert. President Claudia Sheinbaum urged coastal residents of Jalisco, Colima, Nayarit and Michoacan to stay indoors, and Puerto Vallarta's airport was temporarily closed. No official casualty figures have been reported."],"category":"World","tags":["Hurricane Simon","Mexico","NHC","Pacific","Weather"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-hurricane-simon-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated hurricane swirl over a coastline with rain clouds","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated hurricane swirl over a coastline with rain clouds. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"US National Hurricane Center — Hurricane Simon advisories (2026-10-11/12)","url":"https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Reuters — Hurricane Simon report (2026-10-11)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Primary: NHC advisories (latest: Advisory 19, Oct 12 ~02:57 UTC); corroboration: Reuters and CNA. No official casualty figures exist — none cited. Evolving story; numbers reflect the latest advisory at write time. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T06:38:03Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0048-paris-market-fire-2026","slug":"paris-oldest-covered-market-fire-enfants-rouges-2026","headline":"Fire Destroys Paris's Oldest Covered Market, the Marché des Enfants-Rouges","socialHeadline":"The historic Marché des Enfants-Rouges, founded in 1615, was completely destroyed by an overnight fire; no casualties reported","summary":"A fire that broke out in the early hours of Monday, October 12, 2026, completely destroyed the Marché des Enfants-Rouges, Paris's oldest covered food market, officials said. No casualties were reported and the cause is not yet known.","body":["The fire was reported around 4:15am on Monday at the market on Rue de Bretagne in the 3rd arrondissement. The covered hall was completely destroyed and its metal structure partially collapsed inward, according to the Paris fire brigade.","The market, founded in 1615 and listed as a historic monument since 1982, was one of the best-known food destinations in the Haut-Marais, home to stalls serving cuisines from around the world. Its name, meaning \"Market of the Red Children,\" refers to orphans in the area who once wore red clothing.","Ariel Weil, mayor of Paris Centre, said the fire was under control but the market was \"totally destroyed,\" urging people to avoid the Rue de Bretagne area. Lieutenant Colonel Pierre de Bouvier of the fire brigade told reporters \"the market was completely destroyed,\" adding that \"nothing remains of the covered market.\"","No one was injured apart from one firefighter who felt slightly unwell, and officials said the blaze did not spread to neighboring buildings. The cause of the fire has not been established."],"category":"World","tags":["Paris","France","fire","Marché des Enfants-Rouges","historic market"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-paris-market-fire-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated night view of a historic covered market hall with a stylised flame motif above the roofline","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated night view of a historic covered market hall with a stylised flame motif above the roofline. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Paris fire brigade (BSPP) — spokesman Lt. Col. Pierre de Bouvier, statement Oct 12, 2026","url":"https://thehospitalitytribune.com/marche-enfants-rouges-paris-fire/","role":"primary"},{"name":"Mayor of Paris Centre Ariel Weil — official statement, Oct 12, 2026","url":"https://thehospitalitytribune.com/marche-enfants-rouges-paris-fire/","role":"primary"},{"name":"franceinfo — report on the fire (Oct 12, 2026)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x8Pgs8j_vuo","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Primary: BSPP spokesman statement + Mayor of Paris Centre Ariel Weil's official post (both Oct 12). Corroboration: franceinfo, Le Monde/Le Parisien/Le Figaro via roundup, The Sun with Reuters/AFP photography. Zero casualties confirmed by officials; cause unconfirmed — none claimed. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":true,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0049-alvarez-mbilli-riyadh-2026","slug":"canelo-alvarez-mbilli-riyadh-october-31-fight-on-2026","headline":"Álvarez vs M'billi Still On for October 31 in Riyadh Despite Airport Attacks, Promoter Says","socialHeadline":"Turki Al-Sheikh says Canelo Álvarez will fight Christian M'billi in Riyadh on October 31 \"no matter what happens\" after Houthi strikes on the Saudi capital","summary":"Promoter Turki Al-Sheikh said on Sunday that Saúl \"Canelo\" Álvarez still intends to face Christian M'billi in Riyadh on October 31, 2026, despite weekend attacks on the Saudi capital's international airport claimed by the Houthis.","body":["Al-Sheikh, chairman of Saudi Arabia's General Entertainment Authority, said in a social media post on Sunday, October 11, that Álvarez had told him he would \"still fight in Riyadh this October, no matter what happens,\" adding that the Mexican star \"fears nothing.\" Álvarez's camp did not comment.","The bout, billed \"Mexico vs. The World,\" is scheduled for October 31 on DAZN pay-per-view, with the WBC super-middleweight title at stake. Álvarez (63-3-2, 39 KOs) is fighting for the first time since losing to Terence Crawford in September 2025; M'billi (29-0-1, 24 KOs) holds the full WBC title following Crawford's retirement in December 2025.","The reassurance follows a Saturday strike on Riyadh's international airport that killed at least 12 people and wounded more than 300, according to Saudi authorities, with the Houthis claiming responsibility; a second attack on Sunday reportedly killed one more person and injured around a dozen. The figures are consistent with Saudi authorities' reporting of the attacks.","If the fight proceeds as planned, it would be one of the highest-profile sporting events staged in the Saudi capital since the attacks began — and a test of the kingdom's ability to keep its entertainment calendar on track."],"category":"Sports","tags":["boxing","Canelo Álvarez","Christian M'billi","Riyadh","Saudi Arabia"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-canelo-mbilli-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated pair of boxer silhouettes facing off in a ring beneath a stylised championship belt","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated pair of boxer silhouettes facing off in a ring beneath a stylised championship belt. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Turki Al-Sheikh — social media statement via Reuters report (Aadi Nair, Oct 12, 2026)","url":"https://947thebeast.com/2026/10/11/boxing-alvarez-will-go-ahead-with-title-fight-in-riyadh-despite-attacks-says-alalshikh/","role":"primary"},{"name":"USA Today — fight details: fighters, Oct 31 date, Riyadh venue, records (Sept 29, 2026)","url":"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/boxing/2026/09/29/canelo-alvarez-christian-mbilli-fight-date-details/92007185007/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Primary: Al-Sheikh's Oct 11 social-media statement (via Reuters Oct 12). Corroboration: USA Today on fight card details. Casualty figures attributed to Saudi authorities and consistent with art-0045. Fighter willingness reported via promoter only — noted in article. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0050-flyers-worst-start-2026","slug":"flyers-0-5-2-worst-start-franchise-history-fire-tocchet-2026","headline":"Winless Flyers Fall to 0-5-2, Worst Season Start in Franchise History","socialHeadline":"Philadelphia's seventh straight loss to open 2026-27 drew \"Fire Tocchet!\" chants; coach: \"It's on me\"","summary":"The Philadelphia Flyers lost 4-1 to the Carolina Hurricanes on Sunday, October 11, 2026, falling to 0-5-2 — the longest season-opening losing streak in franchise history — as home fans chanted for head coach Rick Tocchet's dismissal.","body":["The 4-1 defeat at Xfinity Mobile Arena was Philadelphia's seventh straight loss to start the 2026-27 NHL season (0-5-2), breaking the franchise record. The Flyers have been outscored 28-8 and are one of three winless teams in the league.","The previous worst season starts in franchise history were six-game winless runs in 1999-00 and 2008-09 — and both of those teams recovered to make the playoffs, a precedent the current group will be hoping to follow.","Frustration boiled over in the third period as sections of the home crowd chanted \"Fire Tocchet!\" and others booed the team off the ice. Tocchet took responsibility afterward: \"We owe the fans a better product on the ice… it's on me, I've got to take the blame.\"","Captain Sean Couturier said the group was struggling for cohesion: \"We're out of sync right now… we're just not winning battles.\" Philadelphia has little time to regroup, with the schedule offering no soft landing."],"category":"Sports","tags":["NHL","Philadelphia Flyers","Rick Tocchet","hockey"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-flyers-record-start-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated crossed hockey sticks and puck above a descending dotted chart line over ice","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated crossed hockey sticks and puck above a descending dotted chart line over ice. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"NBC Sports Philadelphia — report with direct quotes from Tocchet, Couturier, Zegras, Dvorak (Oct 11-12, 2026)","url":"https://www.nbcsportsphiladelphia.com/nhl/philadelphia-flyers/flyers-set-franchise-record-for-longest-losing-streak-to-start-a-season/758177/","role":"primary"},{"name":"AP (Dan Gelston) via 2822news — independent confirmation of record, 0-5-2, prior marks, chants","url":"https://www.2822news.com/sports/ap-sports/ap-flyers-struggle-again-tocchet-has-no-answers-in-franchise-record-7th-straight-loss-to-open-season/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Primary: NBC Sports Philadelphia with direct player/coach quotes. Corroboration: AP independently confirms 0-5-2, record seven-game opening losing streak, prior 1999-00/2008-09 marks, chants. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null},{"id":"art-0051-wnba-finals-venue-2026","slug":"atlanta-dream-wnba-finals-home-venue-uncertain-2026","headline":"Atlanta Dream Still Searching for a Home Venue for the WNBA Finals","socialHeadline":"With State Farm Arena booked for a concert and Hawks games, the Dream's home dates for the 2026 Finals were still undetermined Sunday night","summary":"The Atlanta Dream had still not confirmed where they will play their home games of the 2026 WNBA Finals as of Sunday night, October 11, with their usual home, State Farm Arena, unavailable on the scheduled dates.","body":["The Dream face the Golden State Valkyries in the Finals. The Valkyries will host Games 1, 2, 5 and 7 at San Francisco's Chase Center, an 18,064-seat arena that sold out all season; Atlanta is due to host Games 3, 4 and potentially 6 on October 22, 24 and 29.","State Farm Arena, the Dream's playoff home, is unavailable: a Sombr concert is booked for October 22, and the Atlanta Hawks play the Rockets and Cavaliers on October 24 and 29. The Dream announced last week that all their 2027 home games will be at State Farm Arena, but that does not help this month.","The fallback is Gateway Center Arena in College Park, which seats 3,500 — where the Dream played 16 of their 22 home games this season — though the club is trying to move to a larger venue. Attempts involving Georgia Tech, Georgia State and Gas South Arena have not succeeded, and playoff games at State Farm Arena this year averaged 9,695 fans.","The uncertainty is an awkward subplot for a Finals featuring stars Angel Reese and Rhyne Howard: whichever venue is chosen, thousands of fans who watched the playoff run downtown face a much smaller building."],"category":"Sports","tags":["WNBA","Atlanta Dream","Golden State Valkyries","WNBA Finals"],"author":"NewsVeria Newsroom","publishedAt":"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z","image":{"src":"/images/media-generation-nv-wnba-finals-venue-20261012.webp","alt":"Illustrated empty basketball arena at night with a large question mark over the court","caption":"Illustration: Illustrated empty basketball arena at night with a large question mark over the court. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.","credit":"NewsVeria generated illustration"},"sources":[{"name":"Reuters / Field Level Media — report on venue conflict, dates, capacities (Oct 12, 2026)","url":"https://www.reuters.com/sports/dream-unable-use-hawks-arena-wnba-finals--flm-2026-10-12/","role":"primary"},{"name":"New York Post — independent confirmation via USA Today (Oct 11, 2026)","url":"https://nypost.com/2026/10/11/sports/angel-reese-dream-to-play-wnba-finals-in-3500-capacity-gateway-center-arena/","role":"corroboration"}],"status":"PUBLISHED","verification":{"eventConfirmed":true,"primarySourceFound":true,"independentCorroboration":true,"chronologyChecked":true,"detailsChecked":true,"supersededChecked":true,"imageChecked":true,"reviewer":"NewsVeria editorial desk (AI-assisted, standards in Editorial Policy)","notes":"Primary: Reuters/FLM on conflicts, dates, capacities, undetermined location. Corroboration: NY Post via USA Today. NY Post headline names Gateway Center while Reuters says undetermined — article states undetermined with Gateway Center as fallback. No newer development supersedes.","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z"},"editorPick":false,"breaking":false,"pinned":false,"pinUrl":null}]